   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public health law, in relation to expedited access to medical marihuana in certain cases",
    "basePrintNo": "S5086",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5086-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 59,
       "fullName": "Patrick M. Gallivan",
       "imgName": "427_patrick_m._gallivan.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 427,
       "sessionMemberId": 696,
       "sessionYear": 2015,
       "shortName": "GALLIVAN"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§3360, 3361, 3363 & 3369-b, add §3365-a, Pub Health L",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5086\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the public health law, in relation to\nexpedited access to medical marihuana in certain cases\n\nPURPOSE:  To expedite the availability of medical marihuana.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 Legislative findings and intent\n\nSection 2 adds \"special certification\" to Public Health Law § 3360 as\na certification for a patient whose condition is progressive and\ndegenerative or for whom a delay in the patient's certified medical\nuse of medical marihuana poses a serious risk to the person's life or\nhealth.\n\nSection 3 adds a new subdivision 9 to PHL § 3361 to allow for a\nspecial certification. The Department of Health shall create this form\nand make it available on the Department's website.\n\nSection 4 adds a new PHL § 3365-a which would allow for the expedited\nregistration of registered organizations.\n\nSection 5 amends PHL § 3368-b to allow the commissioner and\nsuperintendent of state police to make a certification limited to\naccommodating expedited access for patients with special\ncertifications and registered organizations under the emergency\nmedical marihuana access program.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:  The purpose of this program is to expedite the\navailability of medical marihuana to avoid suffering and loss of life,\nduring the period before full implementation of and production under\nthe 2014 medical marihuana law, especially in the case of patients\nwhose serious condition is progressive and degenerative or is such\nthat delay in the patient's medical use of marihuana poses a serious\nrisk to the patient's life or health.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY: New Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: None.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:  This act will take effect immediately.\n\n",
